.TH wmagnify 1 "March 22, 2006"

.SH NAME
wmagnify \- magnify parts of the screen

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmagnify
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBwmagnify\fR is a tool which allows you to magnify parts of the screen. The
main difference from \fBxmag\fR is that the image is refreshed automatically,
following the cursor on the screen.

.SH OPTIONS
The following command line options are available:
.TP
.BR \-display " \fIdisplay\fP"
Show the magnified area on this \fIdisplay\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-help
print a help message with the list of options.
.TP
.BR \-m " \fIfactor\fP"
Change the magnification factor, from 1 to 16 (fractions allowed), default is
2. You can change this also while running the program, with the mouse wheel or
the keys described below.
.TP
.B \-noabove
Do not keep the window above the other windows.
.TP
.BR \-r " \fIdelay\fP"
Change the refresh delay, in milliseconds. Default is 33 (30 frames per
second); a frame whose content did not change is not drawn again.
.TP
.B \-smooth
Smooth (bilinear) scaling instead of pixel-perfect.
.TP
.BR \-vdisplay " \fIdisplay\fP"
Take the area to be magnified from this \fIdisplay\fP instead of using the same display as for visualisation.

.SH MOUSE
.TP
.B wheel up, wheel down
Zoom in and out (1x to 16x, in steps such as 1.5x and 2.5x).
.TP
.B middle button
Back to 2x.

.SH KEYS
The following keys can be pressed while \fBwmagnify\fR is running to change its
behaviour.
.TP
.BR 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 ,  5 , 6 , 7 , 8 , 9
Change the magnification factor.
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Zoom in and out in smaller steps.
.TP
.B 0
Back to 2x.
.TP
.B s
Switch between pixel-perfect and smooth scaling.
.TP
.B a
Keep the window above the other windows, or not.
.TP
.BR <space> ", " f
Freeze the camera, making it magnify only the current position.
.TP
.B n
Create a new window.
.TP
.B m
Show/hide the pointer hot spot mark.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WMAGNIFY_STATS
When set, frames per second and the time spent capturing, scaling and drawing
are printed on the standard error every 5 seconds.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xmag (1),
.BR wmaker (1)

